        "math_academy_id": "q-349150",
        "problem": "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}\u27e8{t}^{2}+t,\\,2{t}^{3}-t\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t=\u27e8$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $\u27e9$",
        "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\u27e8{t}^{2}+t,\\,2{t}^{3}-t\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8{\\int }_{-1}^{3}({t}^{2}+t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2{t}^{3}-t)\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component,\n\n$$\n\\int ({t}^{2}+t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFor the second component,\n\n$$\n\\int (2{t}^{3}-t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\u27e8{t}^{2}+t,\\,2{t}^{3}-t\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{-1}^{3},\\,(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{-1}^{3}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(\\frac{1}{3}(27)+\\frac{1}{2}(9))-(\\frac{1}{3}(-1)+\\frac{1}{2}(1)),\\,(\\frac{1}{2}(81)-\\frac{1}{2}(9))-(\\frac{1}{2}(1)-\\frac{1}{2}(1))\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(9+\\frac{9}{2})-(-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}),\\,(36)-0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{40}{3},\\,36\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{40}{3},\\,36\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
